  "articleBody": "It can be tough to know when a storm-damaged interior calls for professional help versus a DIY fix. Here are some clear signs that it's time to bring in the experts:\n\n*   **Gas Odor or Electrical Issues:** If you smell gas, see sparks, or notice any electrical problems, get out immediately and call the utility company and emergency services. This is not a DIY situation.\n*   **Sagging Ceilings or Walls:** These are major red flags for structural damage or significant water accumulation, which can be extremely dangerous. Don't risk it.\n*   **Roof or Structural Damage:** If your roof is compromised or you suspect damage to the main structure of your home, professionals have the equipment and expertise to assess and secure it safely.\n*   **Active Water Intrusion:** If water is still actively entering your home and you can't stop it, or if there's extensive flooding, you need immediate professional water extraction and drying to prevent further damage and mold growth.\n*   **Any Electrical Hazard:** Water and electricity are a dangerous combination. If there's any chance of electrical components being wet, avoid the area and call for professional assistance.\n\nIn these situations, acting quickly to get professional help, like from HH Remodeling LLC, is crucial for your safety and to prevent further damage to your home.",
